Well, yes. But I take that view about most knowledge. Laws of societies
and rules of games (e.g. chess, football, tick/tig/tag/it/he, scissors-
paper-stone) would be the closest analogues. On a drearily empiricist
view they don't exist outside of consciousness, so if you take such a
view then I will grant you the point.

But in my second paragraph quoted above, I do say why language exists
outside the conscious *of the two people engaged in conversation*. So
I did take a swing.

